>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `with_bflags`

``` hol4
HOLFlags.with_bflags : (bflag * bool) list -> ('a -> 'b) -> 'a -> 'b
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Apply a function with boolean flags temporarily set.

A call to `with_bflags [(f1,b1), ..., (fn,bn)] f x` sets each flag `fi`
to `bi`, evaluates `f x`, restores all of the flags to the values they
had beforehand, and returns the result. The flags are restored whether
`f x` returns or raises.

This is the flag-valued counterpart of `Lib.with_flag`, which does the
same for a `ref`. HOL's printing and parsing settings are flags rather
than references, so `with_bflags` is what applies to them; use
`with_flags` for those that take an integer rather than a boolean.

### Failure

Fails if `f x` fails, having first restored the flags. Fails if any
`fi` does not name a trace.

### Example

``` hol4
>> fun print_term_nl tm = (print_term tm; Feedback.HOL_INFO "\n");

>> HOLFlags.with_bflags [(Parse.show_types, true)] print_term_nl ``$=``;

>> print_term_nl ``$=``;
```

